{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the heart of the hasty.</b> From the root of haste in folly." "<b>And the tongue of stammerers.</b> Has no parallel, and in the language of Kedar like עבדים, and the correct interpretation is that it is the opposite of צחות." "And the word <b>צחות</b> lacks [a word], for צחות is an adjective of a noun, and its meaning and its pattern are like זכות."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {2 "Reading טעמו ומשקלו ('its meaning and its pattern'); some witnesses may differ. The missing word he identifies is presumably the noun that צחות modifies."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:17.074784814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}